How to Seize FSMO Roles From Dead Domain Controller?

Mix from:
- https://theitbros.com/transfer-fsmo-roles-from-failed-domain-controller/
- https://petri.com/delete_failed_dcs_from_ad



Important! Before you begin, make sure your account is a member of a following AD groups: Domain Admins and Schema Admins.



from a powershell admin console

# Discover domain controller in the forest
dsquery server -forest


# Check which domain controller is the owner of FSMO
netdom query fsmo

# Before you transfer the FSMO roles on the additional domain controller, 
# you must register the Active Directory schema management library. 
# In case you don‘t, then you won‘t be able to transfer role Schema master.
# !! This must be successful !!
regsvr32 schmmgmt.dll

# Open the utility
ntdsutil

# Enter role management and connect to the domain controller that will be seizing the role/s
roles

connections

connect to server SRV-ADS-DC01.example.com

q

# After connecting to the new target DC, seize FSMO roles
seize naming master

seize infrastructure master

seize rid master

seize schema master

seize pdc

q

# For each role transfer, confirmation is needed
Role Seizure Confirmation Dialog

Are you sure you want server "SRV-ADS-DC01.example.com" to seize the <specific role name> with the value below?

# Enter the cleaning of metadata
#  q back so your prompt is ntdsutil:
metadata cleanup

connections

connect to server SRV-ADS-DC01.example.com

q

metadata cleanup: select operations target
selection operations target: list domains

